# ⚠ .dockerignore, like .gitignore, **does not support end-of-line comments.**
#   `plugin/   # a note` becomes one whole pattern and matches nothing.
#   Four lines below really were that shape, and until it was fixed every build sent
#   plugin/ (263MB), web/ (89MB) and **viewer/ and bench/, which hold real names**
#   into the build context.  A comment must have its own line.

# A separate repository (galaxy-view) · 263MB
plugin/
# The web UI uses its own Dockerfile
web/
# Generated output.  Real personal names are in it in the clear
viewer/
# Real names in the query set's gold labels
bench/
.git/
.omc/
.claude/
.env
.env.local
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
# Created by `go build` on the host (9.5MB) —— it must not enter the build context.
#  ⚠ This line used to be `api/api          # …` —— the very shape the header above warns
#     about, in the file that documents the trap.  Measured 2026-09-01 with two real builds
#     of the same context: with the trailing comment the binary arrives (`-rw-r--r-- 3000000
#     api`); with the comment on its own line the directory is empty (`total 8`).
api/api
